Second mode of transportation we wanted to talk about are city bikes. City bikes, also known by the name veturilo, 
are the best free mode of transportation. There are many bike stations across Warsaw that provide the bikes, but also 
repair stations, which are free of any charges, so you can use them on the city bikes, as well as on your unicycle,
if the need arizes. There are three types of bikes available to people - normal bikes, elecric bikes and tandem bikes.
While most of you are likely familiar with the first two types, the third type is much more unusual. Tandem bikes 
are a type of bikes made for two people to ride simultaneously, without the use of baskets or racks. They have three 
wheels, two sits and two sets of pedals. While it's undoubtly the best type out of the avalable bikes, it's 
unfortunately the one we see the least (because it's so popular obviously). However you need to be carefull when 
chosing this option as it is quite difficult to cross the Independence Avanue while using it - the pedestrian 
bridge that we use to cross it simply too narrow for the tandem bike to make the turns. But it is the best option
in all other circumstances. Veturillo bikes have one big disadvantage - you can only ride them for 20 minutes at 
the time, unless you're willing to pay a fine. On the official site, this fine is simply called a rate at which you 
can lend the bike, but make no mistake, it's a fine for not mannaging your route well enough to be able change your 
bike often enough. You can also be fined for leaving the bike in a wrong place, which, in my opinion, makes more sense
then the other fine. 

